msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/handlers.rst:50
msgid "Everything at once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/handlers.rst:58
msgid "Unknown declared names are simply not passed; a handler that declares a name absent from the context gets nothing for it — use ``**kwargs`` or a default value if you are unsure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/handlers.rst:62
msgid "The first positional parameter conventionally receives the event, but the mechanism is name-based: ``(message)`` and ``(msg=message)``-style names only matter for readability. Anything your handler does not declare is not passed at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/handlers.rst:68
msgid "Message shortcuts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/handlers.rst:70
msgid ":class:`~aiorubi.types.message.Message` carries shortcuts that build and bind API calls:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/handlers.rst:84
msgid "All of them accept the keyword arguments of the underlying ``Bot.send_message`` / ``Bot.send_file`` (``inline_keypad=``, ``chat_keypad=``, ``metadata=``, …). :class:`InlineMessage` provides ``answer(text, **kwargs)`` for reacting to button clicks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/handlers.rst:90
msgid "Class-based handlers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/handlers.rst:92
msgid "Subclass :class:`~aiorubi.handlers.base.BaseHandler` and implement ``handle()``. The class is registered like a function; instantiation happens per update:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/handlers.rst:107
msgid "Available inside ``handle()``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/handlers.rst:109
msgid "``self.event`` — the event object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/handlers.rst:110
msgid "``self.data`` — the whole context dict (including ``state``, filters' injected values, workflow data)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/handlers.rst:112
msgid "``self.bot`` — shortcut property for ``self.data[\"bot\"]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/handlers.rst:113
msgid "``self.update`` — the raw :class:`~aiorubi.types.update.Update` envelope."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/handlers.rst:115
msgid "Class-based handlers are convenient when a handler needs constructor-time configuration shared across updates:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/handlers.rst:128
msgid "Controlling propagation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/handlers.rst:130
msgid "Return normally — the observer stops; no other handler runs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/handlers.rst:131
msgid "Raise :class:`~aiorubi.dispatcher.event.bases.SkipHandler` (or call ``skip()``) — the observer continues with the *next* handler:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/handlers.rst:143
msgid "Returning a :class:`~aiorubi.methods.base.RubikaMethod` from a webhook dispatch answers the webhook with that method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/handlers.rst:146
msgid "A handler may also be registered with no filters at all — it then matches every event of that observer and is typically used as the fallback:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/handlers.rst:156
msgid "Error handlers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/handlers.rst:158
msgid "Exceptions escaping any handler are caught by the built-in :class:`~aiorubi.dispatcher.middlewares.error.ErrorsMiddleware` and routed to the ``error`` observer. The event there is an :class:`~aiorubi.types.error_event.ErrorEvent` wrapping ``exception`` and the original ``update``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/handlers.rst:172
msgid "Combine with :class:`~aiorubi.filters.exception.ExceptionTypeFilter` / ``ExceptionMessageFilter`` (see :doc:`filter`) to specialise."
msgstr ""

